<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco cuts Gulf, Red Sea bunker price.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts Gulf, Red Sea bunker price.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco said it had cut the price of A-960 bunker fuel by $2 a tonne to $125 ($19.19 a barrel) from Gulf ports and also by $2 a tonne to $125 ($19.19) from Red Sea ports, the firm said.</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel grade was raised $11 to $235 a tonne from Ras Tanura and Dammam while liftings from Jeddah and Yanbu were increased by $10 to $235 a tonne.</p>
<p>Prices are effective December 12.</p>
